--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADDENDUM — RESPONSIBLE USE OF HUMAN-SUBJECT DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The AuthGlass dataset contains speech recordings collected from human
participants under a protocol approved by an Institutional Review Board. All
participants provided informed consent for the publication and research use of
their anonymized data. All released recordings are anonymized.

In addition to the license terms above, users of the dataset are asked to
observe the following, consistent with the consent under which the data were
collected:

  1. Do not attempt to re-identify any participant, or to link the recordings
     to any individual or to any other dataset for that purpose.
  2. Do not use the data to build, train, or evaluate systems whose purpose is
     to impersonate a specific individual, or to target individuals.
  3. Redistribute the dataset only together with this license and addendum.

These requests are a condition of the ethics approval under which the data were
gathered, and reflect the expectations of the participants who contributed them.


